                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.154/105: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Guggenheim</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-02-06T11:00:00-05:00">February 6, 1930—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 12:30 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>20. My telegram number 17, February 5, noon. Investigation enables me to say that
                    the present status of Cuban Government finances would not in my opinion justify
                    our Government in raising objection to the proposed Chase loan.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Guggenheim</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
